  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Yacht Club is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Anyone who wants to walk or take a boat to EPCOT or Hollywood Studios.</strong> The layout is the same crescent of hotels as Beach Club, with the same walk and Friendship boats.</li>
      <li><strong>Families of five who don't want a suite.</strong> Official listings show many standard rooms sleeping up to five. In 2026 a Resort View room ran about $648 to $1,138 a night at full price, tax included, a little under Beach Club's starting Resort View rate.</li>
      <li><strong>People who want a steakhouse or a full-service breakfast next door to the room.</strong> Yachtsman Steakhouse and Ale &amp; Compass are in this hotel.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your parks are mostly Magic Kingdom or Animal Kingdom.</strong> Those are buses.</li>
      <li><strong>The nightly rate is the deciding factor.</strong> This is still a Deluxe resort. Water View and Club Level rooms run higher.</li>
      <li><strong>You want the more "beachy" hotel next door, or a Deluxe Room that sleeps six.</strong> Beach Club sells a Deluxe Room category that Yacht Club does not. The two hotels share the pool and much of the dining.</li>
    </ul>
