  <section id="dining">
    <h2>Dining</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ale &amp; Compass Restaurant</strong> is table service for breakfast, lunch and dinner.</li>
      <li><strong>Yachtsman Steakhouse</strong> is the Signature dinner restaurant. Book ahead if that is part of your trip.</li>
      <li><strong>The Market at Ale &amp; Compass</strong> is the quick-service spot.</li>
      <li>Next door at Beach Club: <strong>Cape May Cafe</strong> (character breakfast; confirm dinner) and <strong>Beaches &amp; Cream Soda Shop</strong>.</li>
      <li>The BoardWalk restaurants are a short walk around the lake.</li>
      <li>You can use mobile ordering in the My Disney Experience app at the quick-service spots.</li>
      <li><strong>Park dining reservations:</strong> Disney resort guests can book their whole stay (up to 10 nights) starting 60 days before arrival. Yachtsman Steakhouse and Cape May Cafe can book up, so plan ahead.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: your go-to meal here, and one thing you'd skip.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="pools">
    <h2>Pools and things to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Stormalong Bay</strong> is the shared main pool for Yacht Club, Beach Club and Beach Club Villas. Official pages describe a large, varied complex rather than a single rectangle of water, with both more active and quieter areas.</li>
      <li><strong>Three leisure pools</strong> sit around the Yacht and Beach Club grounds, including one at Beach Club Villas that official pages say Yacht Club guests may use. Official pages also mention whirlpool spas at the pools. The Yacht Club leisure pool is described as sitting in its own garden area.</li>
      <li>Towels are free at the pools. Hours and lifeguard coverage vary and can change.</li>
    </ul>
