  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Start with a Resort View room if the water is not the point.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran about $648 to $1,138 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates. Water View rooms ran about $760 to $1,236.</li>
      <li><strong>Confirm the bed setup if five people need to sleep comfortably.</strong> Official listings allow several combinations, and not every room has a day bed.</li>
      <li><strong>Compare a Yacht Club Resort View room with a Beach Club Resort View room</strong> before you book. The starting 2026 full-price ranges were close, and the two hotels share the pool and much of the dining.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more.</strong> Deluxe rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $35 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="fg-callout">
      <h3>Rates change</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">The rate range above is MouseSavers' October 2026 snapshot of Disney's full prices, not a deal. Always check the live price on Disney's site before you book.</p>
    </div>
